Configure the DePortioner
Insert a Conveyor between the Portioner and DePortioner. The Conveyor transports the portioned
materials in their containers. We used the default settings of the Conveyor.
Configure the DePortioner 
 :
• For the outflow rate we used the default setting of 1 liter per second.
• We selected Fluid Depends On > MU Name so that the DePortioner creates the material and the
amount of the fluid depending on the MU names, which are defined in the Mapping Table.
Configure the DePortioner
Plant Simulation Help 10-403
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• We selected the DataTable named MyTable as our mapping table. We entered the MU name, the
Material, and the Amount of the product, which we want to portion.
• We entered a Set-up Time of 2 minutes to set the DePortioner up for the new product when the product
changes.
• The Entrance Control named partArrives opens or closes the Pipes to the individual Tanks into which
the products flow.
Configure the DePortioner
10-404 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

We typed this source code into the method partArrives:
// entrance control of the DePortioner
if @.MaterialName = "Product X"
   PipeX.PipeOpened := true
   PipeY.PipeOpened := false
   @.MaterialName := "Product Y"
else
   PipeX.PipeOpened := false
   PipeY.PipeOpened := true
end
Insert the Pipes which connect the DePortioner with the succeeding Tanks. Connect the objects with
Connectors.
